\ir routine.sql
\ir view.sql
\ir api.sql
\ir rest.sql

-- The catalogue itself, not only the code that reads it. create.psql has always
-- ended this way; update.psql did not, and the asymmetry meant a routine that
-- raises a newly registered code went live before the code existed.
--
-- What that looks like: exception/routine.sql is part of --update, error/init.sql
-- was not, and the patch that registers new codes runs only under --migrate. So a
-- pull followed by ./runme.sh --update — the day-to-day command, and the default
-- with no arguments — left TokenExpired() raising an identifier absent from
-- db.error_catalog, which answers "Unknown error." in all six locales.
--
-- Safe to repeat: init.sql holds nothing but RegisterError calls, and RegisterError
-- creates what is missing and rewrites the texts of what is not.
\ir init.sql
